       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A visit from the family and a wish to settle things before rounds don't explain why a patient would need 1000 mg of sertraline. That is five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and no standard indication calls for it. It could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Give me 25, 50, 100, or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away. That would still get the order in before the family visit and rounds.\n- **Add a note for review.** I can enter a standard dose and add a note for the team or pharmacy to review titration.\n- **Go through pharmacy or the attending.** If there is a clinical reason for a dose this high, pharmacy or the attending can place or co-sign the order after reviewing it. Sertraline doesn't work faster at higher doses, so if the aim is faster symptom control, they can suggest other options.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
